    "Scouting Notes": "Reliever\n Another interesting indy ball arm the Brewers have discovered\n Striking out 13 per 9 in AA.\n Older for the level\n Fastball velo isn't anything special but rides pretty well through the zone, hasn't had many HR issues with it.\n Best pitch is his curveball which flashes plus at times.\n Slider is his third pitch, and it's not awful, a fringe average offering.\n Have not seen him throw any changeups.\n Command is mediocre. Likely would need to take a step forward to really be a major leaguer, but he's intriguing.\n Age means he is likely running up against the clock here somewhat soon, but he does still have some time.",
